{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wool-indoor-mouse","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observed problem\n`infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` configures `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.voter_errors` with `evaluation_periods = 6`, `datapoints_to_alarm = 3`, and `period = 300`. Its live `alarm_description` heredoc still tells operators it pages on “3 of 5 five-minute periods.” That description is sent to CloudWatch/SNS and contradicts the deployed threshold. The current comment-only sweep cannot edit this HCL value.\n\n## Scope\nCorrect the alarm description to state the configured 3-of-6 window and retain its sustained-versus-transient explanation. Check adjacent alarm descriptions in this file for other threshold text drift. Keep metric identity, thresholds, dimensions, actions, and missing-data behavior unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The CloudWatch alarm description states 3 of 6 five-minute periods and matches the HCL attributes.\n- [ ] A focused test detects future description/threshold drift while respecting the AWS description limit.\n- [ ] Terraform format/validate, focused alarm tests, and repository verification pass.","id":"714b-0b2c-a8f9-468e","parent_id":"","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Voter error alarm description says 3 of 5 while HCL uses 3 of 6"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792758374176967484,"uuid":"d055cf7b-d1aa-4cb7-92fe-45d4ebfea33c"}